ooks to a library in 2011, helping it serve 27,452 people in 2025]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134976044.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[In 2011, Taylor Swift generously donated 6,000 books to bolster local libraries in Berks County amid looming budget cuts. This pivotal support allowed the Reading Public Library to enrich its programs and attract thousands of community members. By 2025, the library circulated over 182,000 items and continued to foster engagement through various initiatives, proving Swift’s contribution remains vital for the region's library services to this day.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-2011-taylor-swift-donated-6000-books-worth-68000-to-a-pennsylvania-library-that-was-struggling-to-stay-open-15-years-later-it-circulated-182228-items-and-drew-27452-program-participants-in-2025/articleshow/134976044.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-2011-taylor-swift-donated-6000-books-worth-68000-to-a-pennsylvania-library-that-was-struggling-to-stay-open-15-years-later-it-circulated-182228-items-and-drew-27452-program-participants-in-2025/articleshow/134976044.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-16T01:08:12+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134976073,imgsize-934832.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Kansas couple transforms backyard into a 100,000-gallon tropical lagoon with six waterfalls]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134975035.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Melissa and Mike Morris dedicated nearly a year to constructing a stunning 100,000-gallon swimming lagoon in Olathe, Kansas. Inspired by the beauty of Tahiti, they created a coastal paradise at home, complete with granite rocks, flowing waterfalls, and vibrant tropical fish. Their captivating project drew attention online, leading to requests for exclusive photo sessions and events, while they relish their private backyard oasis as they finalize the landscaping.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-kansas-couple-wanted-a-beach-without-leaving-home-so-they-turned-two-acres-of-their-olathe-backyard-into-a-100000-gallon-lagoon-with-six-waterfalls-tropical-fish-and-a-23000-pound-boulder/articleshow/134975035.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-kansas-couple-wanted-a-beach-without-leaving-home-so-they-turned-two-acres-of-their-olathe-backyard-into-a-100000-gallon-lagoon-with-six-waterfalls-tropical-fish-and-a-23000-pound-boulder/articleshow/134975035.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-16T00:57:41+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134975990,imgsize-1039068.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Microsoft president Brad Smith says it's ironic that White House targeted his company the same day it gave a medal to former H-1B Satya Nadella]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134975510.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/microsoft-president-brad-smith-says-its-ironic-that-white-house-targeted-his-company-the-same-day-it-gave-a-medal-to-former-h-1b-satya-nadella/articleshow/134975510.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/microsoft-president-brad-smith-says-its-ironic-that-white-house-targeted-his-company-the-same-day-it-gave-a-medal-to-former-h-1b-satya-nadella/articleshow/134975510.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-16T00:41:31+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Poulomi Ghosh</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134975556,imgsize-72214.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Mahomes and Kelce’s jerseys sold for $250,000, helping raise $3.97 million for childhood cancer]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134973976.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[The Kansas City Chiefs stars, Patrick Mahomes and Travis Kelce, showcased their commitment to charity by donating signed jerseys that sold for a remarkable $250,000. This generous contribution is part of the Big Slick Celebrity Weekend, which successfully raised $3.97 million for pediatric cancer initiatives at Children's Mercy Hospital, bringing total donations to over $21 million since the event's launch in 2010.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-2024-travis-kelce-and-patrick-mahomes-put-their-game-worn-chiefs-jerseys-into-a-kansas-city-charity-auction-the-nfl-package-sold-for-250000-as-big-slick-raised-3-97-million-for-pediatric-cancer/articleshow/134973976.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-2024-travis-kelce-and-patrick-mahomes-put-their-game-worn-chiefs-jerseys-into-a-kansas-city-charity-auction-the-nfl-package-sold-for-250000-as-big-slick-raised-3-97-million-for-pediatric-cancer/articleshow/134973976.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-16T00:03:59+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134974301,imgsize-542023.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Yemen claims over 700 Houthis killed after 1,250 strikes rained within 24 hours]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134973857.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Yemen armed forces reported conducting 1,250 targeting operations against Houthis in one day. These strikes coincided with Houthi attacks on Aden’s presidential palace, resulting in casualties. Houthi spokesperson denied claims of missile strikes towards Medina, asserting their innocence. Meanwhile, the Saudi-led coalition intercepted several missiles aimed at its territories amid ongoing tensions. Overall, hostilities between the Houthis and Saudi Arabia have intensified over recent months.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/middle-east/yemen-says-1250-strikes-rained-on-houthis-within-24-hours-claims-over-700-houthis-killed/articleshow/134973857.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/middle-east/yemen-says-1250-strikes-rained-on-houthis-within-24-hours-claims-over-700-houthis-killed/articleshow/134973857.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-15T23:24:13+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Pranjal Pandey</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134973970,imgsize-528653.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Indiana teen brothers, 15 and 14, rescue grandmother and two children from pond; toddler revived]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134972338.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[During a tense moment in Carmel, Indiana, two brothers displayed extraordinary bravery by rescuing a grandmother and her grandchildren from a pond. Their ordeal began when a pushchair slipped into the water, triggering panic. The older brother dove in, employing life-saving measures that successfully revived a two-year-old boy who had momentarily lost consciousness. The brothers will receive community recognition for their courageous actions at the next city council meeting.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/two-indiana-teen-brothers-15-and-14-jumped-into-a-retention-pond-to-save-a-grandmother-and-two-young-children-one-pulled-a-submerged-2-year-old-from-a-stroller-and-got-the-toddler-breathing-again/articleshow/134972338.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/two-indiana-teen-brothers-15-and-14-jumped-into-a-retention-pond-to-save-a-grandmother-and-two-young-children-one-pulled-a-submerged-2-year-old-from-a-stroller-and-got-the-toddler-breathing-again/articleshow/134972338.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-15T23:22:13+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134973912,imgsize-770293.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Cuban-American family’s $119.4 million Expedia verdict overturned by judge]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134973480.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/a-cuban-american-family-claimed-cuba-seized-its-island-in-1959-won-a-119-4-million-verdict-against-expedia-companies-then-saw-a-judge-overturn-it/articleshow/134973480.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/a-cuban-american-family-claimed-cuba-seized-its-island-in-1959-won-a-119-4-million-verdict-against-expedia-companies-then-saw-a-judge-overturn-it/articleshow/134973480.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-16T01:30:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134973889,imgsize-1301655.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[From Tehran's pupils to missile makers: Why Houthis are a bigger threat now]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" 